  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The concept of 'slow travel' has gained popularity in recent years, particularly among environmentally conscious tourists. This approach to travel involves staying longer in one place and exploring its surroundings on foot or by bike. By doing so, travelers can experience the local culture more deeply and develop a greater appreciation for the area's natural beauty.\n\nIn addition to reducing carbon emissions from air travel, slow travel also allows visitors to support local economies more effectively. By choosing accommodations and restaurants that are locally owned and operated, tourists can contribute directly to the community's well-being.\n\nHowever, critics argue that slow travel can have its drawbacks. For instance, it may lead to overcrowding in popular destinations, which could compromise the very essence of the experience. Furthermore, some argue that slow travel is often a luxury only affordable for those with more disposable income, thereby exacerbating existing social inequalities.\n\nDespite these challenges, proponents of slow travel remain optimistic about its potential benefits. They believe that by adopting this approach to tourism, we can create a more sustainable and equitable travel industry that benefits both the environment and local communities.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the article?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Slow travel reduces carbon emissions from air travel.\", \"Slow travel supports local economies more effectively.\", \"The concept of slow travel has been around for decades.\", \"Slow travel can have its drawbacks, such as overcrowding and social inequalities.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Slow travel supports local economies more effectively.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"According to the article, what is a potential drawback of slow travel?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It leads to overcrowding in popular destinations.\", \"It reduces carbon emissions from air travel.\", \"It only benefits wealthy tourists.\", \"It has no negative effects on local communities.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"It leads to overcrowding in popular destinations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What does the term 'locally owned and operated' refer to in the article?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Accommodations and restaurants that are environmentally friendly.\", \"Businesses that have been in operation for over 10 years.\", \"Companies that are owned by local residents.\", \"Eateries and lodgings that support local economies.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Eateries and lodgings that support local economies.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What can be inferred about the author's attitude towards slow travel?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The author is opposed to slow travel due to its drawbacks.\", \"The author believes slow travel is only for wealthy tourists.\", \"The author thinks slow travel has no benefits, but it's a growing trend.\", \"The author is optimistic about the potential benefits of slow travel.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"The author is optimistic about the potential benefits of slow travel.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What does the author suggest as a way to create a more sustainable and equitable travel industry?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Reducing carbon emissions from air travel.\", \"Increasing tourism in less popular destinations.\", \"Adopting slow travel practices, which support local economies.\", \"Implementing stricter regulations on tourist activities.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Adopting slow travel practices, which support local economies.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
